  "question": {
    "text": "Let the solution curve of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, intersect the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
